## Summary

The forward-coverage rule ("new source files must have corresponding new test files", #1310 / #3514) can be satisfied by test files that don't test anything. In a consumer build, the agent produced 26 test files; 15 of them are placeholders that either read the source file as a string and check that certain identifiers appear in it, or assert that an export is a function.

## Environment

- `@deftai/directive` 0.118.1, consumer project (`.deft/core/` deposit layout)
- Host: Grok Build, ceremony tier `rapid`
- Greenfield Next.js 16 + Vitest app built from a single prompt

## Observed

Examples from the consumer repo:

```ts
// src/app/vehicles/[id]/page.test.ts
it("supports edit and delete of the vehicle and its records", () => {
  const source = readFileSync(join(dir, "page.tsx"), "utf8");
  expect(source).toContain("deleteVehicleAction");
  expect(source).toContain("deleteServiceAction");
});

// src/components/shell.test.ts
it("exports a component", () => {
  expect(typeof Shell).toBe("function");
});
```

Same pattern in `middleware.test.ts`, `app/actions.test.ts`, `app/page.test.ts`, `app/layout.test.ts`, every `app/**/page.test.ts`, `components/*.test.ts`, `lib/types.test.ts`.

The 11 remaining files are real (e.g. 21 behavioural tests on `lib/garage.ts`, disk round-trip on `lib/file-store.ts`).

## Why it matters

Gate Integrity (#3156) forbids clearing a red gate by editing the gate. This is the adjacent loophole: the gate wasn't edited, it was fed. A file-count check can't distinguish a real test from a string search, so the framework reports forward coverage that isn't there.

## Suggested direction

One thin fail-closed check (per #3265), e.g. `deft verify:test-substance`, that flags a test file when:

- it never imports the module it is paired with, or
- it calls `readFileSync` / `fs.readFile` on a path ending in the paired source filename, or
- every assertion is `typeof x === "function"` / `toBeDefined()` with no call into the module.

Warn-first, same as the 90% per-diff threshold, with one remediation string.

## Evidence

Side-by-side write-up of this build vs. a no-framework baseline from the same prompt: available on request.
